    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d656">

                <pb facs="0689" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.248/121</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the
                        Division of Near Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-01-16">January 16, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Murray</hi>: The Greek Minister asked me last
                    night whether the thirty training planes, which Mr. Morgenthau<anchor n="67a"
                        xml:id="d656-f1"/> informed him personally on January 14 would be turned
                    over to the Greek Government by our Navy Department, would have to be paid for
                    in cash by the Greek Government or whether they would be turned over under the
                    stipulations of the pending legislation. He asked if he could have an early
                    reply. Please take the matter up with the Treasury Department, Mr. Philip
                        Young<anchor n="68" xml:id="d656-f2"/> presumably, and ask what explanation
                    should be given to the Minister. When you receive a reply, please inform the
                    Minister directly.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d656-f1" n="67a" xml:id="d656-f1-content">
